WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.375
Viewer Basics explains how to use the system without changing route day records.

2
00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:12.750
Viewer access is intentionally read only.

3
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:19.125
Use the Dashboard to understand active routes, jobs waiting, route risk, and daily readiness.

4
00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:25.500
If an operational value must change, contact an Owner, Admin, or Dispatcher rather than looking for a workaround.

5
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:33.167
Open route and tracking views to understand planned work, Driver progress, estimated arrival, completed stops, and exceptions.

6
00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:40.833
Treat customer location, delivery status, tracking links, and Driver information as operationally sensitive.

7
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:48.500
Share information only through the company channels approved for the route day.

8
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:56.375
Use Proof of Delivery to verify that required delivery evidence is attached to the correct stop.

9
00:00:56.375 --> 00:01:04.250
Depending on policy, the record may include a photo, signature, recipient, note, and timestamps.

10
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:12.125
A Viewer can inspect this evidence but should contact Dispatch or an Admin when a record appears incomplete or incorrect.

11
00:01:12.125 --> 00:01:20.600
Use Reports to review service, efficiency, utilization, route history, and proof completion.

12
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:29.075
Compare trends with the actual operating context.

13
00:01:29.075 --> 00:01:37.550
A single route can be affected by appointments, weather, access, vehicle constraints, or customer changes, so use the event and exception record when interpreting a surprising result.

14
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:46.692
When requesting help, provide the organization, page, route or job identifier, expected result, observed result, visible request ID, and a redacted screenshot.

15
00:01:46.692 --> 00:01:55.833
Do not include passwords, tokens, access codes, signatures, or unrelated customer details.

16
00:01:55.833 --> 00:02:04.975
The public support hub also contains searchable answers for common workflow questions.

17
00:02:04.975 --> 00:02:13.737
Complete the Viewer knowledge check to confirm the role boundary.

18
00:02:13.737 --> 00:02:22.500
Viewer training is optional for launch readiness, but it gives supervisors and customer service teams a safe way to use route visibility without creating accidental route changes.

19
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:32.142
Practice locating one active route, one tracking record, one proof artifact, and one report without changing any data.

20
00:02:32.142 --> 00:02:41.783
If the information does not answer the business question, record the question and ask the appropriate Dispatcher or Admin.

21
00:02:41.783 --> 00:02:51.425
Viewer access is most useful when supervisors and customer service teams know exactly where to look and exactly when an operational owner must step in.
